WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.293
Welcome to Thrustline by ValueBridge: a productivity and time-management app that

2
00:00:05.293 --> 00:00:09.850
opens in your browser, works offline, and keeps your data on your own device.

3
00:00:11.233 --> 00:00:16.168
This is your Today page. The capacity meter shows how much of your free working time

4
00:00:16.168 --> 00:00:20.986
is already planned, so you can spot an overbooked day before it happens. Below it:

5
00:00:20.986 --> 00:00:25.568
your timeline, your Big Three for the day, anything that needs attention, your

6
00:00:25.568 --> 00:00:27.213
habits, and your next alert.

7
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:34.091
Adding a task is as easy as typing a sentence. Thrustline reads the date, the time,

8
00:00:34.091 --> 00:00:39.450
the duration, the priority, the project, the energy level and the reminder as you

9
00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:43.750
type, and shows you what it understood. Press Enter, and it's in.

10
00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:50.278
The Tasks page groups everything by when it's due. Or switch to the priority matrix

11
00:00:50.278 --> 00:00:53.873
to see what to do now, what to schedule, and what to drop.

12
00:00:55.267 --> 00:01:00.429
Press Auto-plan, and Thrustline fits your tasks into free time around your meetings,

13
00:01:00.429 --> 00:01:05.591
by deadline, priority and energy. Deep work goes into your peak hours and light work

14
00:01:05.591 --> 00:01:10.508
later, with a buffer around meetings and your lunch kept clear. Solid blocks are

15
00:01:10.508 --> 00:01:15.117
events, dashed blocks are task time, and you can drag any block to move it.

16
00:01:16.533 --> 00:01:21.430
While Thrustline is open, alerts appear with a chime and a snooze button: before

17
00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:26.573
meetings, before task blocks, a morning briefing, and a shutdown reminder at the end

18
00:01:26.573 --> 00:01:31.653
of the day. The alert centre shows what is coming up in the next twenty-four hours.

19
00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:37.574
The Focus timer runs timed work and break sessions linked to a task, logs the time

20
00:01:37.574 --> 00:01:41.972
against it, and keeps a parking lot for stray thoughts, so you can note them and

21
00:01:41.972 --> 00:01:42.467
carry on.

22
00:01:43.867 --> 00:01:48.612
Habits track streaks and weekly targets. Insights show your focus trend, your

23
00:01:48.612 --> 00:01:53.665
meeting load, and how your estimates compare with the time you log. Thrustline can

24
00:01:53.665 --> 00:01:55.267
pad future plans to match.

25
00:01:57.133 --> 00:02:01.697
End each day with the shutdown checklist, and each week with the weekly review, to

26
00:02:01.697 --> 00:02:02.643
catch loose ends.

27
00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:09.745
In Settings, set your working hours, lunch, peak energy and alert preferences. Copy

28
00:02:09.745 --> 00:02:15.055
a backup whenever you like, or export your calendar to Google, Outlook or Apple

29
00:02:15.055 --> 00:02:18.617
Calendar. Support and licence details are under Help.

30
00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:24.565
Thrustline opens on your phone too. Add it to your home screen and it opens like an

31
00:02:24.565 --> 00:02:28.113
app, with a one-day scheduler and in-app alerts while it is open.

32
00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:35.047
To get started: open the Thrustline file, clear the example data, and set your

33
00:02:35.047 --> 00:02:39.740
working day. Then add your first task. Thrustline, by ValueBridge.
